IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-cgt`
IMPORT `itaa-cgt-formulas`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, ss 102-5, 115-100(c), 115-105, 115-115(2), (3), 118-185 -- worked cases for
-- itaa-cgt-formulas.l4 (24 October 2026).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected results were worked by hand from
-- the text and the formulas transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md, before the encoding was run.
-- The first case is the Act's own Example to s 118-185; the rest are hypothetical.

§ `s 118-185 -- partial main residence exemption`

-- The s 118-185 Example: a $10,000 gain, 365 non-main residence days of 3,650 in the ownership period: "$10,000 x (365 / 3,650)
-- = $1,000".
#ASSERT `What gain do I make on a home that was my main residence for part of the time` 10000 365 3650 TRUE EQUALS `capital gain or loss` 1000
-- A $6,000 loss, 100 of 400 days not the main residence: a $1,500 loss.
#ASSERT `What gain do I make on a home that was my main residence for part of the time` (0 MINUS 6000) 100 400 TRUE EQUALS `capital gain or loss` (0 MINUS 1500)
-- An excluded foreign resident, or an inherited dwelling: s 118-185 does not apply.
#ASSERT `What gain do I make on a home that was my main residence for part of the time` 10000 365 3650 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 118-185 does not apply (not an individual, inherited or held as trustee, or an excluded foreign resident)`
-- No non-main residence days, or all of them: not "part only" -- itaa-cgt.l4's questions.
#ASSERT `What gain do I make on a home that was my main residence for part of the time` 10000 0 3650 TRUE EQUALS `not covered: the dwelling was the main residence throughout, or never (see itaa-cgt.l4)`
#ASSERT `What gain do I make on a home that was my main residence for part of the time` 10000 3650 3650 TRUE EQUALS `not covered: the dwelling was the main residence throughout, or never (see itaa-cgt.l4)`

§ `s 115-115 -- foreign or temporary resident for part of the time`

-- (2): held 1,000 days from after 8 May 2012, 500 of them as an Australian resident (not temporary): 500 / (2 x 1,000) = 25%.
-- All 1,000: 50%. None: 0% (Note 1).
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` TRUE FALSE 1000 500 0 EQUALS `discount percentage` 25
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` TRUE FALSE 1000 1000 0 EQUALS `discount percentage` 50
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` TRUE FALSE 1000 0 0 EQUALS `discount percentage` 0
-- (3): held 2,000 days from before 8 May 2012, resident on that day, 400 apportionable days foreign: (2,000 - 400) / 4,000 = 40%.
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` FALSE TRUE 2000 0 400 EQUALS `discount percentage` 40
-- Held from before 8 May 2012 and a foreign resident on that day: (4) to (6), not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` FALSE FALSE 2000 0 400 EQUALS `not covered: the period starts on or before 8 May 2012 and you were then a foreign or temporary resident (s 115-115(4) to (6))`
-- A $100,000 discount capital gain at 25%: net capital gain 75,000. With $20,000 of losses applied: 80,000 x 75% = 60,000.
#ASSERT `What is my net capital gain as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` 100000 0 TRUE FALSE 1000 500 0 EQUALS JUST 75000
#ASSERT `What is my net capital gain as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` 100000 20000 TRUE FALSE 1000 500 0 EQUALS JUST 60000
#ASSERT `What is my net capital gain as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` 100000 0 FALSE FALSE 1000 500 0 EQUALS NOTHING
